<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BFB launches public offer to buy IFP.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BFB launches public offer to buy IFP.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's Banco Fonsecas &amp; Burnay (BFB) is launching a public offer to buy (OPA) for International Factors Portugal (IFP) at 1,900 escudos per share.</p>
<p>The offer, announced in Lisbon bourse's daily bulletin, covers 332,411 shares and represents 33.2 percent of IFP. There is no minimum limit of shares that must be bought.</p>
<p>The offer expires on September 5.</p>
<p>BFB is part of the Banco Portugues do Investimento (BPI) banking group.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
